      "content": "Mahatma Gandhi (1869–1948)"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Mahatma Gandhi (1869–1948) played a central role in India's independence movement.",
        "Rani Lakshmibai (1828–1858) was one of the earliest prominent figures fighting against British rule.",
        "Bhagat Singh (1907–1931) represented the revolutionary youth phase of the freedom struggle.",
        "The Lal-Bal-Pal trio consists of Lala Lajpat Rai (1865–1928), Bal Gangadhar Tilak (1856–1920), and Bipin Chandra Pal (1858–1932).",
        "Sardar Vallabhbhai Patel (1875–1950) and Jawaharlal Nehru (1889–1964) were key post-independence leaders."
      ],
      "id": "xc2g1a4"
